# local.rules — your Snort rule file for the Snort NIDS Lab.
#
# This is the ONE file you edit in this lab. snort.lua already loads it for you,
# so any rule you add here fires the next time you run Snort against a pcap.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Snort rule anatomy (read this once):
#
#   action  protocol  src_ip  src_port  ->  dst_ip  dst_port  ( options )
#   ------  --------  ------------------      ------------------  ---------
#   |       |         |                       |                   |
#   |       |         where it comes from     where it is going   what to match on
#   |       tcp / udp / icmp / ip                                 + msg, sid, rev...
#   alert / log / drop ...
#
# Every rule needs a unique `sid:` (signature ID). Use sids >= 1000000 for your
# own local rules — that range is reserved for exactly this.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Example / starter rule: alert on ANY ICMP packet (e.g. a ping).
# This is the classic "does my sensor work?" rule. It fires on the ICMP echo
# traffic in /opt/snort-lab/pcaps/icmp.pcap.
alert icmp any any -> any any ( msg:"LAB ICMP packet seen"; sid:1000001; rev:1; )

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Add your own rules below this line.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
